.el .ds Aq '
.TH cbspkg 1 2026-11-10 "sandogasa 0.28.0" "Sandogasa Manual"
.SH NAME
cbspkg \- Package and build for CentOS SIGs in CBS, the way fedpkg does for Fedora
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcbspkg\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Packaging for CentOS SIGs that build in the CentOS Build System (CBS), knowing each SIG\*(Aqs conventions: where its package repos live, which branch builds into which collection, and what its targets and tags are called. Proposed Updates and Hyperscale are known.
.PP
add\-pkg, build, promote and upload\-sources act in CBS or the SIG lookaside in your name; see "Commands run by a person" in sandogasa\*(Aqs README.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.SS cbspkg add-pkg
\fBcbspkg add\-pkg\fR [\fB\-\-branch\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-rhel\fR] [\fB\-\-variant\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-owner\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPACKAGE\fR]
.PP
List a package in the CBS tags its branch builds through, as its first build needs
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPACKAGE\fR]
The package (default: the one the checkout\*(Aqs remotes are for)
.SH SELECTION
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<BRANCH>\fR
The branch whose collection to list it in (default: the one checked out)
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
The package\*(Aqs dist\-git checkout (default: the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-rhel\fR \fI<VARIANT>\fR
A Hyperscale variant to build against RHEL rather than CentOS Stream (repeatable; facebook is the one there is)
.TP
\fB\-\-variant\fR \fI<VARIANT>\fR
A Hyperscale variant to use instead of the branch\*(Aqs: a name (facebook) or branch suffix (hs+fb); repeatable
.SH WRITING
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show each step and its command without running anything
.TP
\fB\-\-owner\fR \fI<USER>\fR
The package\*(Aqs owner in CBS (default: your CBS login)
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
Narrate each step and show its command, pausing before each
.SS cbspkg build
\fBcbspkg build\fR [\fB\-\-branch\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-rhel\fR] [\fB\-\-variant\fR] [\fB\-\-background\fR] [\fB\-\-nowait\fR] [\fB\-\-owner\fR] [\fB\-\-scratch\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.PP
Build the checked\-out SIG branch in CBS: the target, the SIG repo\*(Aqs URL and the commit worked out from the branch
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SELECTION
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<BRANCH>\fR
The branch to build (default: the one checked out)
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
The package\*(Aqs dist\-git checkout (default: the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-rhel\fR \fI<VARIANT>\fR
A Hyperscale variant to build against RHEL rather than CentOS Stream (repeatable; facebook is the one there is)
.TP
\fB\-\-variant\fR \fI<VARIANT>\fR
A Hyperscale variant to use instead of the branch\*(Aqs: a name (facebook) or branch suffix (hs+fb); repeatable
.SH BUILDING
.TP
\fB\-\-background\fR
Build at a lower priority (cbs build \-\-background)
.TP
\fB\-\-nowait\fR
Start the builds and leave them running, printing the command that waits for them
.TP
\fB\-\-owner\fR \fI<USER>\fR
The owner to list a new package under (default: your CBS login)
.TP
\fB\-\-scratch\fR
Build without keeping the result (no tags, no listing needed)
.SH WRITING
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show each step and its command without running anything
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
Narrate each step and show its command, pausing before each
.SS cbspkg config
\fBcbspkg config\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.PP
Set up the GitLab token
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Ask for every setting again, with the saved value as the default: Enter keeps it, a new value replaces it, and \- clears an optional one
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS cbspkg promote
\fBcbspkg promote\fR [\fB\-\-branch\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-rhel\fR] [\fB\-\-variant\fR] [\fB\-\-to\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fINVR\fR]
.PP
Move a build to its collection\*(Aqs next stage (\-testing, then \-release, untagging it from \-testing)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fINVR\fR]
The build to promote (default: the package\*(Aqs newest in each of the branch\*(Aqs collections)
.SH SELECTION
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<BRANCH>\fR
The branch whose collections to promote in (default: the one checked out)
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
The package\*(Aqs dist\-git checkout (default: the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-rhel\fR \fI<VARIANT>\fR
A Hyperscale variant to build against RHEL rather than CentOS Stream (repeatable; facebook is the one there is)
.TP
\fB\-\-variant\fR \fI<VARIANT>\fR
A Hyperscale variant to use instead of the branch\*(Aqs: a name (facebook) or branch suffix (hs+fb); repeatable
.SH STAGES
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI<TO>\fR
The stage to promote to (default: the one after where the build is)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
testing
.IP \(bu 2
release
.RE
.SH WRITING
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show each step and its command without running anything
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
Narrate each step and show its command, pausing before each
.SS cbspkg sig-repo
\fBcbspkg sig\-repo\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-sig\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIMR_URL|PACKAGE\fR>
.PP
Make sure the SIG has its repo for a package, a pull mirror of CentOS Stream\*(Aqs, and push a merge request\*(Aqs change to it
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show each step without doing anything
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
Narrate each step and show its command, pausing before each
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
The dist\-git checkout to push from (default: the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-sig\fR \fI<SIG>\fR
The SIG, for a package name (a merge request is always a Proposed Update)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
hyperscale
.IP \(bu 2
proposed\-updates
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Create the repo without asking
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIMR_URL|PACKAGE\fR>
A CentOS Stream merge request URL (a Proposed Update), or a package name
.SS cbspkg upload-sources
\fBcbspkg upload\-sources\fR [\fB\-\-branch\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.PP
Upload the files a branch\*(Aqs sources names to the SIG lookaside, where CBS fetches them
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<BRANCH>\fR
The branch whose sources to upload (default: the one checked out)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show each step and its command without running anything
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
Narrate each step and show its command, pausing before each
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
The package\*(Aqs dist\-git checkout (default: the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
